course: dictionary
lesson: 12771
title: Ecological: words about living things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ecological comes from ecology, the study of how living things live together and depend on each other and on their surroundings. The ending -ical turns it into a describing word, so ecological means to do with ecology. «The pond is full of frogs, snails and weeds, and each one needs the others to survive.» The pond is an ecological balance, where every living thing has its place.
explain: The word has a second meaning too: caring for nature and the environment. «The farm uses ecological methods, so it does not spray harmful chemicals on the crops.» Here ecological means the farm is careful with nature, not just that it has living things on it.
explain: Read the words around ecological to find out which meaning it has. Words like «habitat», «food chain» or «river» point to living things and their surroundings. Words like «pollution» or «damage» point to harm to nature, and words like «careful» or «protect» point to caring for it.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «harm to nature» fits the sentence, you have understood it. If the sentence still makes sense with a simple meaning, you are on the right track.
fact: Ecology is the study of how living things depend on each other and on their surroundings.
fact: Ecological means to do with ecology, or caring for nature and the environment.
fact: «Ecological damage» means harm done to nature, such as to rivers, forests or animals.
fact: Ecological balance means that living things in a habitat stay in a healthy relationship with each other.
fact: An «ecological footprint» is how much of nature a person or group uses up.
exercise: «The river was polluted, and the fish began to die. It was an ecological disaster.» What does ecological disaster mean? | A fun day out by the river | A kind of fishing boat | *Serious harm to nature and living things | Very cold weather in winter
exercise: «The farm uses ecological methods and never sprays harmful chemicals on the crops.» What does ecological suggest here? | Very fast and noisy | Careless and messy | Only for animals that live in houses | *Caring for nature and the environment
exercise: Ecology is the study of how living things | move only at night | are very large and heavy | cannot be seen with a microscope | *depend on each other and on their surroundings
test: «Each animal in the woodland has a place in the food chain, which keeps the ecological balance.» What is an ecological balance? | A cake recipe for children | A pile of leaves on the ground | A kind of bicycle lock | *A healthy relationship between living things in a habitat
test: «Our class cut down on plastic to reduce our ecological footprint.» What is an ecological footprint? | *How much of nature a person or group uses up | A type of bird that cannot fly | The size of a footprint in mud | A map of the school playground
exam: «The scientists studied the ecological effects of the new dam on the river, its fish and its plants.» What does ecological mean here? | *To do with how living things and their surroundings depend on each other | To do with the speed of cars | To do with cooking and recipes | To do with reading and writing
